  "text": {
    "id": {
      "title": "Traversal tree",
      "story": "Sebuah binary tree ditulis sebagai objek `{ v, l, r }`: `v` adalah nilai, `l` dan `r` adalah anak kiri dan kanan, atau `null` kalau tidak ada. Tree kosong adalah `null`.\nTulis `traverse(tree, order)` yang mengembalikan array nilai sesuai urutan `order`: `\"pre\"` (node, kiri, kanan), `\"in\"` (kiri, node, kanan), `\"post\"` (kiri, kanan, node), atau `\"level\"` (per tingkat dari atas, kiri ke kanan).",
      "hint1": "Tiga urutan pertama hanya berbeda di kapan nilai node dimasukkan: sebelum, di antara, atau sesudah memproses kedua anaknya. Satu fungsi rekursif cukup.",
      "hint2": "Untuk `\"level\"`, pakai antrean: mulai dari akar, ambil node paling depan, catat nilainya, lalu masukkan anak kiri dan kanannya ke belakang antrean."
    },
    "en": {
      "title": "Tree traversal",
      "story": "A binary tree is written as an object `{ v, l, r }`: `v` is the value, `l` and `r` are the left and right children, or `null` when missing. An empty tree is `null`.\nWrite `traverse(tree, order)` that returns an array of values in the given `order`: `\"pre\"` (node, left, right), `\"in\"` (left, node, right), `\"post\"` (left, right, node), or `\"level\"` (level by level from the top, left to right).",
      "hint1": "The first three orders differ only in when you record the node's value: before, between, or after handling its two children. One recursive function covers all three.",
      "hint2": "For `\"level\"`, use a queue: start with the root, take the front node, record its value, then add its left and right children to the back."
    }
  },
